-- title:
--   Deuring: β-[k₀] is p times an endomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field with decidable equality, $p$ a prime with $\mathrm{char}\,k = p$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $k$ which is elliptic. Let $\beta$ be an additive endomorphism of the group $W(k)$ of affine points of $W$ (in the Weierstrass affine model, with point at infinity) which lies in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet k W W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28), i.e. which either is zero or admits a single rational representation: there are bivariate polynomials $n_X, d_X, n_Y, d_Y$ over $k$ and a finite set $B \subseteq k$ of excluded abscissae such that for every nonsingular affine point $(x,y)$ with $x \notin B$ one has $d_X(x,y) \neq 0$, $d_Y(x,y) \neq 0$, and $\beta$ sends $(x,y)$ to $\bigl(n_X(x,y)/d_X(x,y),\, n_Y(x,y)/d_Y(x,y)\bigr)$. Assume integers $t, q$ with $\beta \circ \beta + q\,\mathrm{id} = t\,\beta$ as additive endomorphisms of $W(k)$, and an integer $k_0$ with $p \mid t - 2k_0$ and $p^2 \mid k_0^2 - t k_0 + q$. Then there exists $\gamma$ in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet k W W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) with $\beta - k_0\,\mathrm{id} = p\,\gamma$, the scalar actions being those of $\mathbb{Z}$ on the additive group of additive endomorphisms of $W(k)$.
--
--   This is the arithmetic core of Deuring's description of endomorphism rings in characteristic $p$: a quadratic order generated by an endomorphism satisfying $X^2 - tX + q$ is maximal at $p$, since whenever $(X-k_0)/p$ again satisfies a monic integral quadratic the element $\beta - [k_0]$ is already divisible by $p$ in the ring of geometric endomorphisms. It feeds the passage from endomorphisms to maximal orders used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld material and in the statement that a root of a quadratic relation in the rational endomorphism subring is a multiple of $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_mem_rationalHomSet_sub_smul_id_eq_char_smul_of_dvd_of_sq_dvd.lean

